<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70628" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηδύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ύος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>any
				of the cavities</i> in the body, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>de Arte</u>
				10
			</span></i>: hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>stomach,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.296
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				487
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1263
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>belly, paunch,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.290
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.47
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>bowels,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				757
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i>
			<i>Aër.</i><i><span class="en">
				19
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξελεῖν τὴν νηδύν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.87
				</span></i>
			; as the seat of thirst, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέγξας ἄδιψον νηδύν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Cyc.</u>
					574
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρδῃ τε νηδύν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					207
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>womb,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.496
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				460
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				665
			</span></i>, etc.; also of Zeus when in travail of Athena, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				890
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				899
			</span></i>; of Dionysus, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				527
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. νάρθηκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					272
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέβητος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>L.</u>
					276
				</span></i>
			.—Acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηδύα</span> for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηδύν</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				1.616
			</span></i>; dat. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηδύσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					467
				</span></i>
			. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ</span> in trisyll.
			cases, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηδῠς</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
			</span></i>l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Dian.</u>
				160
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηδῠν</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				356
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				574
			</span></i>: but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηδῡν</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.519
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Alc.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				416
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
			</span></i> l.c.]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
